1
00:00:01,200 --> 00:00:05,000
GAVEL. Every bid is a hold. The hammer is the payment.

2
00:00:05,700 --> 00:00:08,300
Charge a card up front, and bidders hold back.

3
00:00:08,300 --> 00:00:10,900
Leave bids unsecured, and winners walk away.

4
00:00:10,900 --> 00:00:13,400
Shout bids on paper sheets, and the record is hard to trust.

5
00:00:13,800 --> 00:00:18,389
A judge opens /try. One tap starts a sandbox room.

6
00:00:19,039 --> 00:00:23,889
A join code and a ticket QR.

7
00:00:24,539 --> 00:00:31,889
A bidder types the code. Or scans the ticket QR.

8
00:00:32,539 --> 00:00:38,199
Pick a ceiling. The most this bidder may bid.

9
00:00:38,199 --> 00:00:42,003
Hold the button 3 seconds.

10
00:00:42,003 --> 00:00:44,889
Held, not charged.

11
00:00:45,539 --> 00:00:51,889
A second phone joins from the QR link.

12
00:00:52,539 --> 00:00:56,389
The auctioneer opens the lot.

13
00:00:56,739 --> 00:00:59,979
Bids arrive from the phones.

14
00:00:59,979 --> 00:01:03,095
Prices only go up.

15
00:01:03,095 --> 00:01:06,389
Every screen agrees.

16
00:01:07,039 --> 00:01:13,399
Hold the hammer 3 seconds. No accidental sales.

17
00:01:13,399 --> 00:01:15,889
Sold.

18
00:01:16,439 --> 00:01:19,089
The big screen names the winner.

19
00:01:19,739 --> 00:01:23,639
A receipt for every bidder.

20
00:01:23,839 --> 00:01:26,470
With a share link and a QR.

21
00:01:27,120 --> 00:01:30,821
Paste a ledger export.

22
00:01:30,821 --> 00:01:33,751
Chain verified.

23
00:01:33,751 --> 00:01:36,470
Edit one entry. The chain marks it broken.

24
00:01:37,420 --> 00:01:40,420
Kill survived. A real server kill during settlement, on the PayPal sandbox: one capture, two holds voided, a ledger of 19 entries that verifies.

25
00:01:40,420 --> 00:01:43,420
Live voice 24 of 24. Both speech providers answered 24 of 24 synthetic clips through the live socket. No bid accepted without a confirm.

26
00:01:43,420 --> 00:01:46,420
Ledger verified. Every bid joins a hash chain. Anyone can check it again, and an edited entry is marked.

27
00:01:46,420 --> 00:01:49,320
Latency, honestly. Hammer to captured p95 3.8 s against a 2.5 s target. Hammer to settled p95 6.9 s against 6 s. Both missed.

28
00:01:49,620 --> 00:01:53,836
The ledger lab. A 30 day simulated ledger in an AG Grid table.

29
00:01:53,836 --> 00:01:56,470
Edit one entry and the chain marks it.

30
00:01:57,320 --> 00:02:05,320
A key. HTTP. JSON. Create a room, bid and read the ledger from the Judge API.

31
00:02:05,620 --> 00:02:09,470
The docs list every call.

32
00:02:10,420 --> 00:02:12,920
G3 in progress. The honor-period probe is still timing. The final reading is about 12 Nov.

33
00:02:12,920 --> 00:02:15,420
G5 partial. Speech is measured on synthetic, noise-free audio only.

34
00:02:15,420 --> 00:02:18,020
Sandbox only. No real money moves.

35
00:02:19,520 --> 00:02:24,020
Built by Harsh Bhanushali and Dhairya Patel. gavel.dualmindlab.tech. docs.gavel.dualmindlab.tech. github.com/harshbhx/gavel-auction. PayPal sandbox only.
